      "expression_templates": {
        "lcl_pressure": {
          "params": [
            "tt",
            "qq",
            "pp"
          ],
          "description": "Pressure of the lifting condensation level of a parcel at (tt, qq) on pressure level pp, by one Newton step along the dry adiabat: pp + dq/(dq_sat/dT dT/dp), with dq = min(0, qq - q_sat) the parcel's sub-saturation (non-positive, so the result lies above pp), q_sat the capped saturation mixing ratio with its virtual-temperature correction, dq_sat/dT the liquid-fraction blend of the two Clausius-Clapeyron factors, and dT/dp = R_d T/(cp p). cutypen's cloud-base block, which places the base at whichever adjacent half level is nearer this pressure.",
