        {
          "id": "step918_col1_shallow_ascent",
          "description": "cutypen's shallow test parcel, step 918, TILE COLUMN 1 of 2: the parcel is NOT LAUNCHED: the surface virtual-temperature flux is downward (buoy_flux >= 0), so no level is reached and every array is left as cuinin handed it. Reference: the real64 replay of the chem170 single-column run (em_scm_xy, Weisman-Klemp sounding, dx = 20 km, 59 levels, dt = 60 s, cu_physics = 16) through kernels/ntiedtke_driver of WRF fork branch earthsciml-instrumented-chem170, the sh_* tape spliced in at the end of cutypen's shallow phase (fork commit 177342a5); the seven cu_ntiedtke_init arguments at binary64, the scheme's literals at their binary32 roundings (FORTRAN_BUGS N109). Inputs: the environment the ascent saw (sh_*), cuinin's parcel (ci_*) and the TEACHER TRAJECTORY sh_ptu/sh_pqu/sh_dh, from which each level is stepped (see the component description). Algebraic observeds at t = 0 with no ODE state; the empty time_span is one static evaluation. Arrays are compared as Linf errors at 1e-9 of each profile's maximum (the project baseline for a double-precision kernel reference); labels, levels and the type are integers compared exactly.",
